Requirements: 4   with obligations: 4

[task-01] The text output of `acceptance decompose` shows, for every obligation it
    lists, which kinds of evidence that obligation requires (its `required_evidence`
    value), placed inside the bracket that already carries the obligation's type and
    derivation, for example `[test_demand/explicit, tests_only]`. Where an obligation
    carries a `required_evidence_reason`, the output prints that reason beneath the
    obligation's restated text. An obligation that is `satisfied_by_absence` is marked
    so a reader can tell it apart from one that is not.
    -> show-required-evidence-in-bracket  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       The text output of `acceptance decompose` shows each listed obligation's
       `required_evidence` value inside the bracket that already carries the
       obligation's type and derivation.
    -> print-required-evidence-reason-beneath-restated-text  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       Where an obligation carries a required_evidence_reason, print that reason beneath
       the obligation's restated text.
    -> satisfied-by-absence-marked  [invariant/explicit]
       Mark obligations that are satisfied by absence so a reader can tell them apart
       from obligations that are not.

[task-02] A regression test asserts each of these three things against a decomposition
    fixture.
    -> decomposition-fixture-regression-test  [test_demand/explicit]
       A regression test asserts each of these three things against a decomposition
       fixture.

